ul.li:
Configure an MCP OAuth connection to
                  Atlassian JIRA Cloud by using the simpler default authorization flow, where the
                  MCP server handles app registration during
                  authorization:{
  "servers": {
    "atlassian": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.atlassian.com/v1/mcp/authv2",
      "oauth": {
        "redirect_uri": "https://your.webauthor.server/oxygen-xml-web-author/plugins-dispatcher/web-mcp-auth/callback"
      }
    }
  }
}

Configure an MCP OAuth connection to GitHub by
                  using your own GitHub application. If you create an application on the provider
                  side, you can place the OAuth client credentials directly in the configuration so
                  that the MCP server does not need to dynamically register an application during
                  authorization:{
  "servers": {
    "github": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/",
      "oauth": {
        "client_id": "YOUR_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID_HERE",
        "client_secret": "YOUR_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET_HERE",
        "redirect_uri": "https://your.webauthor.server/oxygen-xml-web-author/plugins-dispatcher/web-mcp-auth/callback"
      }
    }
  }
}
